<div>
    <p>Browses and edits every real PHP lang file this app has — global (<code>lang/</code>/<code>resources/lang/</code>), every enabled module's own (<code>{module}::</code>), and the Nexus core package's own (<code>nexus::</code>) — grouped by file, with a per-group completion percentage against every published <a href="{{ route('nexus.module.action', ['module' => 'Language', 'action' => 'index']) }}">Language</a>.</p>
    <p>All the actual reading/writing is <code>Nodex\Nexus\Services\DirectTranslationService</code> — that class already existed in the core package, singleton-bound and already reading the Language model, before this module's admin screens were built. This is only the UI on top of it.</p>
    <p>Saving writes straight back to disk: an app-owned module's own file gets edited directly; core/vendor namespaces are written to <code>lang/vendor/{namespace}/{locale}/{file}.php</code> instead — Laravel's real translation-override path, checked ahead of the original file automatically, so the original module/package source is never touched.</p>
    <p>No test writes into a real module's own <code>resources/lang</code> — that would risk corrupting actual shipped translations under test. The vendor-override write path is exercised against a disposable, self-cleaning fixture namespace instead; the destructive-adjacent parts (writing over a real module's files) are, like in the old ZentaraStartProject module's own admitted gap, unverified by an automated test.</p>
</div>
